# Response headers for the whole site. Cloudflare consumes this file and does not serve it.
# Hand-written like wrangler.toml and .assetsignore; build_static.py only sweeps stale *.html,
# so it survives a rebuild.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. The site had no security headers at all. It is static, it loads nothing
# from a third party and it reflects no user input, so the odds of an injection are already
# low. What raises the stakes is that a buyer's season password lives in localStorage: any
# script that ever runs on this origin can read it and post it somewhere. Most of the value
# below is in the outbound half of the CSP, which is what turns "an injection happened" into
# "an injection happened and could not phone home".
#
# 'unsafe-inline' is unavoidable for now: every page carries inline <style>, inline <script>
# and onclick handlers, all generated by app.py. Hashes or a nonce would be the stronger
# answer and would mean changing how PAGE is assembled. Even with it, default-src/connect-src
# 'self' still blocks loading or reaching ANY other origin.
# form-action carries api.web3forms.com because the contact form POSTs straight there; it is
# a plain HTML form post, so NOTHING is added to script-src or connect-src and no third-party
# code runs on this origin. If the contact form is ever removed, take that host back out.
#
# CLOUDFLARE WEB ANALYTICS (2026-08-09). The 2 cloudflareinsights hosts below are what let the
# page-view beacon run: it loads from static.cloudflareinsights.com and POSTs to
# cloudflareinsights.com, and WITHOUT BOTH the browser silently blocks it and you collect
# nothing. This applies to Cloudflare's automatic edge injection too, which inserts the same
# script tag, so there is no setup path that avoids needing them.
#
# This is the first third-party SCRIPT ever allowed to run on this origin, which is the exact
# thing the paragraph above says the outbound CSP exists to prevent, so it deserves its
# reasoning written down. The season password in localStorage is readable by any script on
# this origin, and beacon.min.js would be such a script.
#
# It is still the right call, because Cloudflare is already inside the trust boundary
# completely: they serve every byte of this site. Anyone able to tamper with beacon.min.js can
# already rewrite the pages themselves, so the marginal trust being extended here is close to
# zero. That reasoning does NOT generalise. A beacon from any company that is not already the
# host would be a real new party on the origin and should be refused on these grounds.
#
# connect-src gains only cloudflareinsights.com, an endpoint that reports to Cloudflare and
# hands nothing back to an attacker, so the "could not phone home" property survives for every
# destination that matters. If analytics is ever switched off, take both hosts back out.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://api.web3forms.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000; includeSubDomains

# The paid payload. Fingerprinted in every page's fetch URL (?v=<sha256[:12]>) and read with
# cache: "force-cache", so it is safe to cache hard; a new build changes the URL.
/locked/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# The shared stylesheet and search index, lifted out of the pages 2026-08-06. Both carry
# ?v=<sha256[:10]> in every <link>/<script>, so the URL changes whenever the content does
# and these can be cached hard. Without this they would revalidate on every page view and
# most of the point of extracting them (one download for a whole visit) would be lost.
/site.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/players.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
